# Create README
print_status "Creating README.md..."
cat > README.md << EOF
# $PROJECT_NAME

Documentation site built with Nextra and Next.js, powered by native Podman.

## Quick Start

### Development

Use the native Podman runner script:

\`\`\`bash
./podman-run.sh
\`\`\`

The site will be available at \`http://localhost:3000\`.

### Background Mode

Start services in the background:

\`\`\`bash
./podman-run.sh start
\`\`\`

### Production

Run with nginx proxy:

\`\`\`bash
./podman-run.sh prod
\`\`\`

Access the site at \`http://localhost:3000\` or via nginx at \`http://localhost:8080\`.

## Native Podman Commands

The \`podman-run.sh\` script provides these native Podman operations:

\`\`\`bash
./podman-run.sh dev      # Interactive development server
./podman-run.sh start    # Background/detached mode  
./podman-run.sh prod     # Production with nginx proxy
./podman-run.sh logs     # View real-time container logs
./podman-run.sh status   # Check service status and health
./podman-run.sh stop     # Stop all running services
./podman-run.sh cleanup  # Remove all containers, networks, and volumes
./podman-run.sh help     # Show all available commands
\`\`\`

## Project Structure

\`\`\`
$PROJECT_NAME/
├── pages/              # Documentation pages (MDX files)
│   ├── docs/           # Main documentation
│   ├── api/            # API documentation  
│   └── index.mdx       # Home page
├── components/         # Custom React components
├── public/             # Static assets
├── theme.config.tsx    # Nextra theme configuration
├── next.config.js      # Next.js configuration
├── podman-run.sh       # Native Podman runner script
├── nginx.conf          # Nginx proxy configuration
└── PODMAN_GUIDE.md     # Podman-specific documentation
\`\`\`

## Pure Podman Features

- **No Docker dependencies**: Uses only native Podman commands
- **Cross-platform**: Optimized for both macOS and Linux
- **SELinux support**: Automatic SELinux compatibility on Linux
- **Local caching**: Smart volume strategies per platform
- **Production ready**: Built-in nginx proxy support
- **Service management**: Easy start/stop/status operations

## Resources

- [Nextra Documentation](https://nextra.site)
- [Next.js Documentation](https://nextjs.org/docs)
- [Podman Documentation](https://docs.podman.io)
- [MDX Documentation](https://mdxjs.com)
- [Podman Desktop](https://podman-desktop.io)
EOF

# Create Podman guide
print_status "Creating Podman guide..."
cat > PODMAN_GUIDE.md << 'EOF'
# Native Podman Guide for Nextra

This guide covers using Nextra with pure Podman commands - no Docker or Docker Compose dependencies.

## Features

### ✅ What This Setup Provides

- **Pure Podman**: No Docker or Docker Compose dependencies
- **Cross-platform**: Optimized for both macOS and Linux
- **Smart caching**: Platform-specific volume strategies
- **Production ready**: Built-in nginx proxy support
- **Service management**: Easy container lifecycle management
- **SELinux support**: Automatic compatibility on Linux systems

## Command Reference

### Basic Operations
```bash
# Start development server (interactive)
./podman-run.sh dev

# Start in background
./podman-run.sh start

# Stop all services  
./podman-run.sh stop

# View real-time logs
./podman-run.sh logs

# Check service status
./podman-run.sh status
```

### Production Operations
```bash
# Start with nginx proxy
./podman-run.sh prod

# Access URLs:
# - Development: http://localhost:3000
# - Nginx proxy: http://localhost:8080
```

### Maintenance Operations
```bash
# Rebuild with latest images
./podman-run.sh rebuild

# Complete cleanup
./podman-run.sh cleanup

# Show all available commands
./podman-run.sh help
```

## Resources

- **Podman Documentation**: https://docs.podman.io/
- **Nextra Documentation**: https://nextra.site/
- **Podman Desktop**: https://podman-desktop.io
EOF

print_success "Nextra project '$PROJECT_NAME' created successfully!"
print_status "Pure Podman setup complete - no Docker dependencies!"
echo ""
print_status "Next steps:"
echo "  1. cd $PROJECT_NAME"
echo "  2. ./podman-run.sh          # Start development server"
echo "  3. Open http://localhost:3000 in your browser"
echo ""
print_status "Available commands:"
echo "  ./podman-run.sh dev      # Development mode (default)"
echo "  ./podman-run.sh start    # Start in background"
echo "  ./podman-run.sh prod     # Production with nginx proxy"
echo "  ./podman-run.sh logs     # View container logs"
echo "  ./podman-run.sh status   # Check service status"
echo "  ./podman-run.sh stop     # Stop all services"
echo "  ./podman-run.sh cleanup  # Clean up all resources"
echo ""
print_status "Pure Podman features:"
echo "  ✅ No Docker or Docker Compose dependencies"
echo "  ✅ Native Podman commands for maximum compatibility"
echo "  ✅ Automatic OS detection and optimization"
if [[ "$OSTYPE" == "darwin"* ]]; then
    echo "  ✅ macOS: Uses local cache directories for best performance"
else
    echo "  ✅ Linux: SELinux-compatible with named volumes"
fi
echo "  ✅ Production mode with nginx proxy support"
echo "  ✅ Systemd service generation capability"
echo ""
print_status "To start editing:"
echo "  - Add new pages in the 'pages/' directory"
echo "  - Edit theme.config.tsx for site configuration"
echo "  - Add custom components in the 'components/' directory"